{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 39, :comments ["<b>And you shall see it.</b> This excludes a nighttime garment — or does it perhaps exclude only a blind person's garment, since it says וזכרתם? It gives seeing to one who sees and remembering to one who does not see. Another explanation: וראיתם אותו — if you do so, it is as though you see the Throne of Glory, which resembles tekhelet, as Rabbi Meir said: How is tekhelet different from all kinds of dyes? Because tekhelet resembles the firmament, and the firmament resembles the Throne of Glory, as it is said: ״ויראו את אלהי ישראל ותחת רגליו כמעשה לבנת הספיר״, and sapphire is crystal in the vernacular, which resembles the firmament. And it is written וראיתם, and then וזכרתם, and then ועשיתם — this teaches that seeing brings to remembrance, and remembrance brings to action." "<b>And you shall remember all the commandments of HaShem.</b> Rashi explains: the numerical value [gematria] of tzitzit, as our Rabbis taught, etc. And even though ציצת is written defective [without] the second yod, it can be answered that ציצת is written three times, and one of them is written לציצת, and the lamed completes the three missing yods. And furthermore I have heard that some make loops and windings until all the loops and windings and threads and knots of all four tzitziyot add up to 613. And the measure of a loop in [the matter of] tekhelet is enough to wind, double, and triple, and one who reduces should not reduce below 7, corresponding to the 7 firmaments, and one who adds should not add beyond 13, corresponding to the 7 firmaments and the 6 airs between them." "<b>And you shall not wander after your hearts and after your eyes.</b> As the Master said: the heart and the eye are the two agents of sin."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:09:35.479886975Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}